{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/queue/next.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:36:38.617597Z","id":"be5745164e0e181363a840b1310f6e7e67edfe2ac31b472e27204e01ffeef1d4","body":{"detail":"A turn failed for the network sets waitingFor: claude and emits one ProbeClaude (update.dart TurnFailed). Its answer ClaudeReachable(false) leaves the job waiting with no further probe until Woke(foreground: true) (update.dart Woke). Task 25's EffectRunner (with ApiConnection) has to keep watching and send ClaudeReachable(true) when the connection is back, or jobs waiting on Claude stay waiting while the app is in the foreground. Alternatively a Tick could re-probe on a backoff.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":325},"end":{"line":329},"content_hash":"e70163bea29427fd4d844631bdd3bb8f2162c5dd1e3571caa3123ac98310ad30"},"summary":"The queue probes Claude once per wait: after ClaudeReachable(false) it probes again only on Woke(foreground: true), so the runner must send ClaudeReachable(true) when Claude answers again","tags":["queue","runner","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/queue/update.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:46:34.562669Z","id":"d9219b9f88c077cf3e74de2914b014b272179b725892ad57d10ab8178d326702","body":{"detail":"Failure: a job's publish step is refused doc_moved (a document of the plan moved), the job moves to failed, the app is killed or relaunched (the worker isolate restarts), and the person taps Retry: MoveJob(→ running) lands, the row's step is still turn:<n>, JobLocal.results (not durable) no longer holds the finish call's refusal, so next() emits Publish(publish:<base>) with the same PublishPlan and its stale document pins; the core refuses doc_moved again and the job fails again. Retry never reaches a model turn; only Discard helps. Checked with a scratch test (not committed): JobsLoaded([failed row, error doc_moved, steps turn:2 = finish base 0]) on an empty model, then Retry and the running row: the effects are [Publish#102(j, publish:0, done), KeepAlive, PublishState]. The unit test 'a moved document fails the job; Retry re-plans without publishing' (apps/clax_app/test/queue/update_test.dart:396) passes only because the same worker keeps the refusal in JobLocal.results. The same holds for a change's Reply or a CommitStep refused Invalid (update.dart:547-555, e.g. invalid_thread after the thread's delete): the job fails, Retry repeats the same deterministic write, and it fails again. The refusal that decides the next turn is local state; the row only says error doc_moved, and Retry clears that (next.dart:175-178).","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":496},"end":{"line":511},"content_hash":"fc07572ae2bb9eb6d19292346bd4e5a99f63d3e15e888e7fcc072e48606b4509"},"suggested_fix":"Make the refusal part of the row: next() answers turn n's finish call from the row when the job's error names it (keep error on the Retry MoveJob and let the next CommitStep's patch clear it, or record the refused attempt as the result of a step such as publish-refused:<base>), so a fresh worker answers the call with refused('doc_moved', path) and starts turn n + 1. For an Invalid refusal of a Reply or CommitStep, Retry should re-plan (a new turn) rather than repeat the write. Add a test that runs the Retry on a model rebuilt from JobsLoaded alone.","summary":"A job failed doc_moved is not re-planned by Retry after a worker restart: the finish call is published on the same plan again and fails doc_moved again, every time","tags":["review","queue","task-24","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/queue/next.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:46:34.562765Z","id":"290941f188301df67c9ff474c633b6ff908521b4ec6c77184082eaf2f9d41358","body":{"detail":"Failure: a make's turn calls ask, the Ask lands (job waiting, question q1 open), the app is killed and relaunched, then the person answers q1: the core moves the job to running with questions {q1: answered}; the new worker's JobLocal.asked is empty, so next() emits Ask(j, turn 1, a1) again (checked with a scratch test, not committed: the effects after the answered row are [Ask#102(j, turn 1, a1), PublishState]). The Ask docs (effect.dart:112-115) leave it to the runner to 'ask once per job, turn and call', but the store gives it no way to: questions dedupe on (session, tool_use_id) (crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs:690, :378), the relaunched worker registers a new session (spec 2026-10-19-in-process-core-design §8.1), and job_questions keeps no call (crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs:272-277, JobQuestion {question_id, answer}). So the runner creates a second question and the person is asked the same thing twice. The property test cannot see this: FakeJobsCore mints the question ID from the job, turn and call (apps/clax_app/test/queue/core_answers.dart:69), which the real store does not do, and it creates the question inside the Ask rather than refusing an unknown one as ask_job_question does (jobs.rs:807-860).","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":274},"end":{"line":284},"content_hash":"9e4b073042ae955b07d9a9f8f949c67164af43b5327e881b61031d373b4c8a2c"},"suggested_fix":"Put the call in the row: have JobFull's questions carry the question's tool_use_id (a join on questions, no schema change), have the runner create each ask question with tool_use_id = turn:<n>/<callId>, and derive asked in next() from job.questions instead of JobLocal.asked (delete that field). Make FakeJobsCore mint opaque question IDs and keep the tool_use_id, so the property test exercises the restart. A kill between the question's creation and its PUT still leaves one orphan that the old session's reaping withdraws; record that as a waiver.","summary":"After a restart the queue asks a job's question again: the call-to-question map is local, and the store cannot tell the runner which question a call asked","tags":["review","queue","task-24","store","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/queue/update.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:46:34.562829Z","id":"c14ac298fa1ae63418883b7065ada29a07eaae7c440cc935bf5ec33237eb9590","body":{"detail":"OutOfTime sets intent pause on running and waiting jobs only (update.dart:261-272). When the first MoveJob(→ paused) is answered, the running count drops and next() (next.dart:126-130) emits MoveJob(→ running) for a queued job, followed by KeepAlive(true) once it lands. Checked with a scratch test (not committed): three running jobs and one queued, OutOfTime, then each pause committed: the first Committed emits [StopWork(r), MoveJob(q → running @1), PublishState]. The OS's time is out, so the new job's turn is killed and resumed at the next launch: a wasted model turn and a job shown running that is not. Spec §7.6 says jobs running out of time are paused; it does not say new ones start.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":261},"end":{"line":272},"content_hash":"f519cb9c2ee51839c8ba8daf7416244189bc71b11370157c6238a68d369813d9"},"suggested_fix":"Model the suspension: a QueueModel field (e.g. suspended: bool) set by OutOfTime and cleared by Woke(foreground: true) or a launch, under which nextJob starts nothing (no move to running from queued or paused, no StartTurn). Add the case to update_test.dart and to the generator.","summary":"OutOfTime starts queued jobs: each pause that lands frees a slot, and the resume table moves the next queued job to running while the app is being suspended","tags":["review","queue","task-24","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/queue/model.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:46:34.562962Z","id":"fef2ee9c6f73438bd6929d4dce37d517eddd400e62118a0798ee5439a3caf955","body":{"detail":"(1) QueueModel.loaded is a bool beside owner, so loaded: true with OwnerNone or OwnerClaiming can be built; canWrite (next.dart) checks both. (2) coreOpen is set by CoreOpened and read nowhere. (3) JobLocal's waitingFor, renderTries and renderDeadline (model.dart:206-215) are independent: a deadline with no Render in flight, or renderTries 1 while waiting for Claude, can be built; and the deadline is kept per job while Tick reads it per in-flight Render effect (update.dart Tick). (4) Job.step is String? and StepKey.parse runs at each use; an unparsable step makes _run do nothing, silently (next.dart:193-196). (5) OwnerClaiming.heard is a Set<bool> standing for two flags (a release heard, a claim or drain end heard). (6) ClaimOwner is not recorded in inFlight, so an OwnerClaimed answering a claim made before a CoreOpened is taken as the new claim's (it then meets not_owner and claims again; harmless, but not matched). (7) A Make or Change waiting in pending is absent from viewOf until the jobs load, though spec §7.2 says the snapshot includes jobs in flight to the core.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":340},"end":{"line":395},"content_hash":"ddc9f82ddda1dde6c03e0ecf5ce69cc3c9cb1c7a3243a51acc57f9d097981b61"},"suggested_fix":"Owner: OwnerNone | OwnerClaiming(heardRelease, heardHeld) | OwnerLoading(token) | OwnerHeld(token), dropping loaded; drop coreOpen; JobLocal.render: RenderIdle | RenderInFlight(effect, tries, deadline?) | RenderWaiting; parse step to StepKey? at the codec and keep it typed in Job; show pending creations as queued in viewOf.","summary":"The model can still hold states that mean nothing: loaded apart from the owner, a dead coreOpen, the render's three loose fields, a step string re-parsed at every use","tags":["review","queue","task-24","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/queue/next.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:46:34.563012Z","id":"74e392b6be6a4538f61c6ff13dae6ffc52bafc63443f562a5e25ee7d2d7a84d1","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-19-in-process-core-design §8.1 says a reply step names the session that published the job's version, which OPEN_JOB_SESSIONS (crates/clax-store/src/sessions.rs:223) keeps from the reaper; the step acknowledges that session's feedback on the threads. Reply(id, jobId, reply) carries only the finish call's ReplyPlan (next.dart:199-203), and after a relaunch the worker's own session is new. commit_reply_step accepts any live session (crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs:1636-1642), so a runner that names its own session commits, but acknowledges nothing of the publishing session's feedback. The store needs nothing new for step marks or a new app's ID (begin_publish_step mints and keeps the artifact, jobs.rs:1474-1530, and a make's Publish with no artifact ID is what it expects); the session is the one link the queue leaves to the runner.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":199},"end":{"line":203},"content_hash":"f63d7ce68f160248d1788f294c14de586f5e62ad014356aaa22882ba0af9a0ab"},"suggested_fix":"Either let commit_reply_step take the session from the job's publish step (the version's session_id), so the body names none, or give Reply the PublishStepResult (artifact and version) for the runner to read the version's session; test it in Task 25's runner_test against a relaunch.","summary":"A change's Reply names no session, so after a relaunch the runner has to find the session that published the version on its own","tags":["review","queue","task-24","runner","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/queue/next.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:46:34.563430Z","id":"65746b0b488d6b859b9de2d039caa411c3ec0bb6913de5e1314b1c975682bd41","body":{"detail":"Checked with a scratch test (not committed): a running job with claude unreachable, JobsLoaded emits ProbeClaude; after ClaudeReachable(false), four Ticks a minute apart emit nothing. Time already arrives as Tick (QueueModel.now), so a retry schedule belongs in the model: keep probeAt (or a backoff step) in QueueModel, set it at ClaudeReachable(false), and probe on the Tick that passes it; the same deadline also frees `probing` if a ProbeClaude is never answered, which today leaves probing true and stops every later probe (next.dart probe()). The runner then only answers ProbeClaude and cannot strand jobs waiting on Claude.","kind":"comment","references":"be5745164e0e181363a840b1310f6e7e67edfe2ac31b472e27204e01ffeef1d4","summary":"Confirmed, and the model can own this instead of the runner: after ClaudeReachable(false) no Tick probes again","tags":["review","queue","task-24","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/queue/update.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:35:33.568119Z","id":"f7ca2bd1d98e1e2066e7023213a48a32882ff7e4375f7f70d0f2394d4cdbef25","body":{"detail":"Evidence: apps/clax_app/test/queue/update_test.dart 'after doc_moved / version_moved / not_rendered_clean / an invalid publish / a refused reply / a refused turn commit, a worker rebuilt from the rows does what the live one does' (six tests) pass: a model rebuilt from JobsLoaded alone, then Retry, emits the same job effects as the live worker and no Publish or Reply. With the row answer disabled in next.dart (scratch, reverted) four of them and 'a moved document fails the job; Retry re-plans without publishing' fail. crates/clax-store jobs::tests::a_committed_step_clears_the_error_of_the_step_before_it passes (bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all). No schema change: error_json already holds JSON, so migration 46, its fixture and JOBS_TABLES are unchanged.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2ac881088","summary":"Fixed in 2ac881088: a refused publish, reply or turn commit is recorded in the row (error {code, detail, step}) before anything plans from it; Retry keeps it, the next committed step clears it (crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs commit_step and insert_step); next() answers the refused finish call from the row","supersedes":"d9219b9f88c077cf3e74de2914b014b272179b725892ad57d10ab8178d326702","tags":["reason:fixed","queue","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/queue/next.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:35:34.257826Z","id":"1f9ab02a178f2323286f8dd0b41783e86b61d9b67ba10508a5d33b35dfde7036","body":{"detail":"The tool call names the job as well as turn and call: one session asks for every job, and the store dedupes questions on (session, tool_use_id), so turn:<n>/<call ID> alone would hand a second job the first one's question (refused invalid_question at its PUT). Evidence: apps/clax_app/test/queue/update_test.dart 'a worker relaunched while its job waits asks nothing again' failed before the change (the relaunched worker emitted Ask#5(j, turn 2, a1) and FakeJobsCore, which now mints opaque IDs per session and tool call, created a second question) and passes after; 'a worker rebuilt from the rows alone answers the call from its question' passes; crates/clax-store jobs::tests::open_jobs_lists_steps_threads_and_questions asserts tool_use_id. The orphan left by a kill between creation and PUT is recorded as a waiver on apps/clax_app/lib/queue/effect.dart.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ec7dad849","summary":"Fixed in ec7dad849: JobFull.questions carries each question's tool_use_id (join on questions), the Ask's question is created with tool_use_id <job>/turn:<n>/<call ID>, and next() finds it in the row; JobLocal.asked and Committed.questionId are gone","supersedes":"290941f188301df67c9ff474c633b6ff908521b4ec6c77184082eaf2f9d41358","tags":["reason:fixed","queue","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/queue/update.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:35:34.691255Z","id":"3617dc11d2b1563320c82481a632c2b59e727875cb9b37d8637c8f333293a025","body":{"detail":"Evidence: apps/clax_app/test/queue/update_test.dart 'rule 10b: out of time, the queue is suspended running jobs pause, and nothing starts until the app is in the foreground' failed before the change (Actual: MoveJob(q -> running @1), MoveJob(s -> running @1) after the pauses landed) and passes after; the property test's 'suspended' coverage key is reached.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:aeef47d4e","summary":"Fixed in aeef47d4e: QueueModel.suspended, set by OutOfTime and cleared by Woke(foreground: true), under which the resume table pauses what runs and starts nothing","supersedes":"c14ac298fa1ae63418883b7065ada29a07eaae7c440cc935bf5ec33237eb9590","tags":["reason:fixed","queue","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/queue/model.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:35:35.615566Z","id":"b894d64c2bc4e0738c1c565e314609438a507dcf40164f68ecc13063296727d1","body":{"detail":"The render is one state: in flight is its Render effect (last, deadline), waiting is JobLocal.waitingFor render; renderTries and renderDeadline are gone. Evidence: apps/clax_app/test/queue/update_test.dart 'an answer to a claim made before the core reopened counts for nothing', 'intents wait for the jobs, shown queued, then run' and the resume table row 'running, a step the queue does not know -> failed invalid_step' pass, and each failed with its behaviour removed in a scratch copy (reverted): 3 failed of 120.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e1c877561","summary":"Fixed in e1c877561: OwnerLoading/OwnerHeldBy replace loaded, coreOpen is gone, StepKey is parsed once (UnknownKey fails a running job invalid_step), OwnerClaiming has heardRelease/heardHeld and names its claim, which OwnerClaimed/OwnerHeld/OwnerDraining answer, the Render effect carries its last try and deadline, and viewOf shows pending Make/Change as queued","supersedes":"fef2ee9c6f73438bd6929d4dce37d517eddd400e62118a0798ee5439a3caf955","tags":["reason:fixed","queue","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/queue/next.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:35:36.085300Z","id":"972ccad6669f2c11e36368deb833075559c891b541a560eba1b7836ee7d67310","body":{"detail":"Evidence: crates/clax-store jobs::tests::a_reply_step_after_a_relaunch_comes_from_the_session_that_published (a new session registered after the publish; the reply's session is the publishing one and its feedback row is acknowledged) and a_reply_step_needs_the_jobs_publish_step_and_its_live_session pass; crates/clax-server tests/api_jobs.rs a_reply_step_replies_resolves_and_acks_once passes (bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__1 --test_arg=api_jobs::, 16 passed), including 400 for a body naming session_id and the agent comment from the publishing session's harness after a relaunch under another.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7fa5157fa","summary":"Fixed in 7fa5157fa: commit_reply_step takes the session from the version of the job's last publish step (versions.session_id), the reply body names none, and the Reply effect carries no session","supersedes":"74e392b6be6a4538f61c6ff13dae6ffc52bafc63443f562a5e25ee7d2d7a84d1","tags":["reason:fixed","queue","store","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/queue/next.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:35:36.670265Z","id":"5a241ff979195969e26a944aed420ef4bdde9503d8c87b1282fc41945eb20f03","body":{"detail":"Evidence: apps/clax_app/test/queue/update_test.dart 'after Claude does not answer, the worker probes again on its clock' and 'a probe never answered is let go at its deadline, and asked again' failed before the change (no ProbeClaude at the 30 s Tick) and pass after; the property test's 'probe let go' coverage key is reached. This closes the reply 65746b0b with it.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:267c46284","summary":"Fixed in 267c46284: QueueModel.probe (idle, inFlight(effect, deadline), after(at)) re-probes on the Tick 30 s after ClaudeReachable(false) and lets go of a probe not answered in 30 s; the runner only answers ProbeClaude","supersedes":"be5745164e0e181363a840b1310f6e7e67edfe2ac31b472e27204e01ffeef1d4","tags":["reason:fixed","queue","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/queue/effect.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:35:37.141549Z","id":"ea940d93831ea6154ec8f9b229553d6101409bd31bc88ff584ef2afcdcff1a31","body":{"detail":"Ask has the runner create the question (POST /api/questions, tool_use_id <job>/turn:<n>/<call ID>) and then PUT /api/jobs/{id}/questions/{qid}. The store dedupes questions by (session_id, tool_use_id) (crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs BY_TOOL_USE), and a relaunched worker registers a new session, so a kill between the two calls makes next() emit Ask again and the person sees a second question until the first's session ends (its reaping withdraws it: the job does not hold it, so OPEN_JOB_SESSIONS does not keep that session). Accepted: the window is one round trip, and closing it needs the question created and recorded in one transaction (a store route that does both).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":122},"end":{"line":139},"content_hash":"fbf7770acd594beb492385a3eb9bd7969125b1bcfffb7828aa86d38969d8b66f"},"summary":"A worker killed between creating an Ask's question and recording it in the job leaves one question no job holds; the relaunched worker asks again from its new session","tags":["queue","runner","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/queue/worker_main.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:37:59.252468Z","id":"cdbc21bdcebd152d16b23afad39620414c5df0b8967eff2652bd89e52829676c","body":{"detail":"The client and worker share an isolate group (Isolate.spawn), so sending the immutable Msg and QueueState objects works today. codec.dart (plan docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-19-in-process-core.md, Task 25) is to encode Msg/Effect/QueueState as JSON-able maps; once it lands, QueueWire's four methods should call it (or be replaced by it) so a worker on another engine or group gets plain data.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":34},"end":{"line":47},"content_hash":"15cd597afa0b85edb6ffd243042e30c8d5054e74c210859692521f948810867e"},"suggested_fix":"Implement QueueWire.intent/readIntent/state/readState with codec.dart's encode and decode, and keep isolate_client_test.dart passing.","summary":"QueueWire passes intents and states across the isolate boundary as themselves; lib/queue/codec.dart's encoding is to replace it","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/queue/worker_main.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:37:59.252608Z","id":"d421bc1583f5d64f378d7a7b79a78da96548a8ab075c83a66fa4c16572101157","body":{"detail":"The plan's workerMain (Task 25 Interfaces) subscribes to topics jobs, questions and threads and turns events into JobNoticed, OwnerChanged and CoreOpened. Here the loop dispatches CoreOpened once at start and leaves the subscription to WorkerRunner (through WorkerContext.core and WorkerContext.send), since the claim (CoreJobs.claim(streamId)) needs the subscription's ready ID. A runner that never subscribes leaves the worker deaf to OwnerChanged releases and to rows written elsewhere.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":179},"end":{"line":202},"content_hash":"d8799029ccd688d2dd933a75e8fafedb170d9edfc4d8628a5992d01bbf2df29d"},"suggested_fix":"When runner.dart lands, either have its factory open the subscription and feed its events through WorkerContext.send, or move the subscription into workerMain and hand the stream ID to the runner.","summary":"workerMain does not subscribe to the core's events or read the stream ID the owner claim needs; the runner the factory builds must","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/queue/isolate_client.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:37:59.252676Z","id":"68692ab634aaf17c1af5256322db504d9d7364567cee92aa267188d55793830e","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-19-in-process-core-design §7.2 says settings and key changes are intents too, and the plan's QueueClient has settingsChanged and keyChanged, but lib/queue/msg.dart has no such Intent. IsolateQueueClient.start takes settings and apiKey once; a restarted worker gets the same snapshot.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":40},"end":{"line":52},"content_hash":"1ba8c9a1d789395f044e3734064644cf5c0e57787dc7e5b3d3257bd3afd8ecb6"},"suggested_fix":"Add SettingsChanged/KeyChanged intents (or worker-side messages) and keep the client's snapshot current so a restarted worker spawns with the newest.","summary":"Settings and key changes after spawn never reach the worker: it holds the snapshot it was spawned with","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/queue/isolate_client.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:37:59.252723Z","id":"965b3a92acd58863ebf3b1e4842cfe8ec3cb735dce6e406ab6329e8e58292fea","body":{"detail":"viewOf (lib/queue/model.dart) fills JobView.error with JobError.code for failed and cancelled jobs. After a second worker death within a minute, IsolateQueueClient._stop sets error to the whole sentence \"Clax's builder stopped. Restart Clax to go on.\" on every job that is not done or cancelled, keeps its state and clears its offers. A UI that maps error codes to text would not recognise it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":180},"end":{"line":203},"content_hash":"df241d419ca4841d9427663fdb62f8382fc54800ab3038a0020ff11abc84c2dc"},"suggested_fix":"Give JobView a field for the queue being stopped (or a code such as builder_stopped the UI words), and have the UI show the sentence from it.","summary":"A stopped queue puts the sentence builderStopped in JobView.error, which otherwise carries an error code","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
